VECTOR_DISTANCE 
			Computes exact numeric similarity between two vectors.
			Computes distance between two vectors (cosine, Euclidean, dot product).
			Used in exact KNN search (full table scan).
			Slow for large datasets.
			When to use it - Small tables, Precise similarity scoring, Ranking results manually, Debugging embeddings

VECTOR_SEARCH 
			VECTOR_SEARCH( table.vector_column, query_vector, top_n, metric )
			Performs a full similarity search using a vector index, returning the top‑K nearest neighbors efficiently.
			Uses a vector index (DiskANN) to perform fast nearest‑neighbor search.
			Returns top‑K similar rows.
			Designed for large-scale AI workloads.
			When to use it - Large datasets (millions of rows), Real‑time semantic search, RAG pipelines, Recommendation systems
			  
VECTOR_NORMALIZE() 
			Transforms a vector so that its magnitude becomes 1.
			This is essential for: cosine similarity, semantic search, embedding comparison, vector indexing, stable distance metrics
			
VECTORPROPERTY 
			Returns metadata about a vector column or a vector index.
			It does not compute similarity, distance, or search results.
			Instead, it tells you how the vector is stored, indexed, and configured.
			
VECTOR_SEARCH → retrieves the rows
VECTOR_DISTANCE → computes the score for each row

CONTAINSTABLE → 
			precise, structured, Boolean full‑text search 
			“Search for exact terms using rules.”
 
FREETEXTTABLE → 
			natural‑language, concept‑based search
			“Search for meaning using language.”
			

- Exact nearest neighbor (k-NN) search involves calculating the distance between a query vector and all vectors in your dataset, then returning the k closest matches. 
	This method guarantees precise results but can be computationally intensive for large datasets.
			


			
